  "rationale": "Deploying mfa:admin blocks both auth_dc and auth_adfs, making admin_dc and admin_adfs unreachable. Therefore stolen_dbadmin cannot be obtained, blocking authentication to the database, fileserver, and backup and preventing all exfiltration techniques. With no controls, an attacker can phish a workstation, pivot internally, authenticate to the appserver, steal admin credentials through kerberoasting, authenticate to and escalate on the DC, dump database-admin credentials, and then access and exfiltrate the database. Thus zero controls are insufficient and one is sufficient."
 },
